  "schoolyard": 1,
  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has broad, maple-like leaves that can be used to teach about leaf structure and function. Its distinctive, mottled bark peels away in patches, providing a hands-on example of tree growth and health. The round, spiky seed balls hang from long stems and can be used to explain seed dispersal mechanisms. This tree's adaptability to urban environments makes it a practical example of plant resilience and urban ecology.",
